  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45452\"], \"answer\": \"This matches a known issue: Command Palette can keep intercepting a hotkey that was assigned to a top-level command, even after the extension was uninstalled, and this blocks that shortcut system-wide (Ctrl+W in the past ticket). Disabling Command Palette frees the key again, which matches what you see with Ctrl+B. To fix it, close Command Palette and open %localappdata%\\\\Packages\\\\Microsoft.CommandPalette_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\\\LocalState\\\\settings.json. In the \\\"CommandHotkeys\\\" array, look for an entry with \\\"ctrl\\\": true and \\\"code\\\": 66 (the key code for B). If it is there and you don't need it, delete that entry, and the shortcut should work again right away. If no such entry exists, your problem may have a different cause, so please upload a PowerToys bug report ZIP and your settings.json.\"}",
